cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Merge-RL: Iterative Reward Design for Autonomous Merging on highway-env"
abstract: >-
  A study in reward shaping for autonomous merging in dense traffic, comparing
  sparse collision-only rewards against a dense time-to-collision (TTC) based
  safety signal. Multi-seed evaluation (n=3) demonstrates a 58% relative
  reduction in crash rate (Welch's t-test, p=0.024) and tighter cross-seed
  variance for the TTC variant. Includes documentation of six failure modes
  encountered during development, including a single-seed result that
  overstated the baseline by 26 percentage points.
